2. **Black-Box AI Hiring & Resume Filtering (e.g., Workday, Eightfold AI):** Rejected job applicants receive canned rejection emails without knowing thousands of qualified candidates over age 40 or with non-standard syntax were systematically filtered out by the same underlying ML engine. Local nodes issue dual CCPA Inference DSARs and EEOC Disparate Impact requests (under 29 C.F.R. Part 1607). Non-compliance triggers Harm Beacons, allowing litigation capital to assemble multi-employer class actions against the central software vendor.

3. **FinTech & Payday Lending Risk Scoring:** Borrowers facing exorbitant, dynamic interest rates or sudden credit denials are subject to secret automated underwriting inferences. Issuing statutory inference DSARs forces FinTech lenders to disclose secret scoring models or incur statutory violations. Harm Beacons aggregate borrowers across states, exposing predatory lending patterns without requiring centralized client intake.

4. **Dynamic Price Discrimination & Surge Behavioral Engines:** E-commerce, hotel, and ride-share platforms execute dynamic price discrimination based on inferred willingness-to-pay metrics (device type, battery level, location history). Local nodes demand the exact “behavioral pricing inferences” used during specific transactions. Non-compliance generates Harm Beacons that aggregate isolated consumer price markups into nationwide consumer protection lawsuits.

